interface or a peripheral, he says, is more likely plain IP reuse. The new blocks are

00:08:03.320 --> 00:08:04.460
where HLS landed.

00:08:04.960 --> 00:08:09.300
Problems not tackled before, where someone still has to pick a hardware architecture.

00:08:09.960 --> 00:08:14.720
Badru Agarwala of RISE design automation gives the productivity figure in that piece.

00:08:15.340 --> 00:08:20.600
HLS handles complex control and data path with 10 to 20 times less code than RTL.

00:08:21.180 --> 00:08:26.140
Less code is easier to review, which is how he says you trust what you ship, and easier

00:08:26.140 --> 00:08:27.460
to edit when the spec moves.

