00:10:00.620 --> 00:10:06.100
Dave Kelf at Breaker Verification System says HLS now has real value for a specific kind

00:10:06.100 --> 00:10:11.940
of design, and that a historic barrier, the same one logic synthesis once had, was the gap

00:10:11.940 --> 00:10:15.860
between the abstract model, especially timing and the finished circuit.

00:10:16.480 --> 00:10:20.260
Engineers struggle to make that connection, and that made the result hard to trust.

00:10:20.760 --> 00:10:26.920
Demura sets a field failure next to a clean lab run, a design can pass a full 100% regression

00:10:26.920 --> 00:10:32.100
and still fail in the field, and then someone has to understand how it works in order to fix it.

00:10:32.500 --> 00:10:39.440
He says it took a long time before HLS was trusted, because people in that seat have been burned by circuits they did not understand.

00:10:40.060 --> 00:10:43.100
The rules that keep the output recognizable have been stable.

00:10:43.100 --> 00:10:49.720
Club says the synthesizable subset of C++ and by extension system C has stayed relatively

00:10:49.720 --> 00:10:52.200
constant for the last 10 to 15 years.

00:10:52.700 --> 00:10:57.920
Streaming interfaces in an untime sequential language needed IP, because the language does

00:10:57.920 --> 00:10:59.600
not show explicit concurrency.

00:11:00.200 --> 00:11:05.500
Siemens built AC channel and bit accurate data types, so streaming could live inside that subset.

00:11:06.240 --> 00:11:09.540
Mahir Aurora at Chip Agents reads the whole climb as a bargain.

00:11:09.540 --> 00:11:16.640
For 50 years, EDA progress meant climbing abstraction, RTL, and then HLS, because a person

00:11:16.640 --> 00:11:18.480
cannot hold the full design space.

00:11:19.020 --> 00:11:23.380
Abstraction narrows the space so an engineer can reason about it, and that narrowing

00:11:23.380 --> 00:11:25.100
cost potential quality of result.

00:11:25.780 --> 00:11:28.720
HLS, in his line, was never about better hardware.

00:11:29.260 --> 00:11:31.560
It was the price of designing for human capacity.

00:11:32.120 --> 00:11:36.520
Take a block new enough to miss the IP shelf and walk the article's ratio through it.

00:11:36.520 --> 00:11:40.500
The description is 10 to 20 times shorter than the RTL it replaces.

00:11:41.040 --> 00:11:43.840
So review and a spec change land on the short text.

00:11:44.340 --> 00:11:49.480
Sea level checks, orders of magnitude faster than RTL checks, are what would let an agent

00:11:49.480 --> 00:11:51.740
try architectures before a net list exists.

00:11:52.480 --> 00:11:57.620
The output still has to be implementable RTL that meets power, performance and area inside

00:11:57.620 --> 00:11:58.740
a defined context.

00:11:59.440 --> 00:12:01.940
Nandie's comparison is the bill on that last step.

00:12:01.940 --> 00:12:08.560
The HLS result is the one that was not hand-optimized, so the power sits higher than crafted RTL.

00:12:09.020 --> 00:12:13.320
If the block was a bus or a peripheral, clubs' path never entered this flow.

00:12:13.880 --> 00:12:21.800
IP reuse was the likely answer, and the 10-20 times saving was never on offer, because that code was not going to be written either way.

00:12:22.300 --> 00:12:24.480
The repair is where this choice stops paying.

00:12:24.480 --> 00:12:30.240
When a 100% regression still fails in the field, Demure's case, the short description

00:12:30.240 --> 00:12:34.780
has already shipped, and the fix needs the timing connection KELF says engineers have

00:12:34.780 --> 00:12:36.020
always had trouble making.

00:12:36.640 --> 00:12:41.780
It also stops paying when the power envelope cannot take nandies unoptimized result, and

00:12:41.780 --> 00:12:46.700
when a generator leaves the synthesizable subset, Club says has held for 10 to 15 years.

00:12:47.280 --> 00:12:52.340
Outside that subset, the circuit is no longer one those rules taught an engineer to recognize,

00:12:52.340 --> 00:12:58.600
and Aurora's 50-year bargain, a smaller space held by a person no longer covers the repair.

